<title>CHINA: Shanghai Volkswagen produces 800,000th Santana.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Volkswagen produces 800,000th Santana.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 800,000th Santana sedan, one of China's most popular cars produced by the Shanghai Volkswagen Automotive Co, has rolled off the production line, Xinhua news agency said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The Santana has 54 percent of China's sedan market and has become popular for taxi companies as well as individuals, the agency said.</p>
<p>Shanghai Volkswagen is a joint venture between Germany's Volkswagen AG and Shanghai Automotive Industry Corp.</p>
<p>Annual production capacity is 300,000 cars a year, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>For the year to date, the company has produced 96,606 Santanas, of which 45,684 were the new Santana 2000 model, it said.</p>
